           APPLICANT.

       COALITION FOR CLEAN AFFORDABLE ENERGY’S MOTION TO FILE
           TESTIMONY IN SUPPORT OF STIPULATION OUT OF TIME

COMES NOW the Coalition for Clean Affordable Energy ("CCAE") pursuant to 1.2.2.12

NMAC and requests the Commission to allow it to file its Testimony in Support of Stipulation

Out of Time. In support of this Motion, CCAE states as follows:


1.     CCAE inadvertently missed the filing deadline, incorrectly recording the due date, for its

Testimony in Support of Stipulation and requests an additional day to submit the Testimony on

July 2, 2026.


2.     No party is prejudiced by granting this Motion.


3.     The positions of the parties are as follows: no objection exists from any party in this

proceeding (SPS, Staff, Walmart, Targa, FEA, NMLCG, and EMNRD).


WHEREFORE, for the reasons stated herein, CCAE respectfully requests the Commission to

allow it to file its Testimony in Support of Stipulation out of time and for such other relief as is

just and reasonable.
 Respectfully submitted this 1st day of July 2026.


